// Interop: foreign code declared in Heron, the JS host that runs it, how
// data crosses, when it runs, the protocol, and packaging.
include = [
  "./declaring.heron",
  "./host.heron",
  "./data_mapping.heron",
  "./timing.heron",
  "./protocol.heron",
  "./packaging.heron",
]

@lens(user, developer)
| Behaviour that needs a real language, declared in Heron and written in that language: how it's bound, the [JS host](#language.interop.host.js_host) that runs it, how data crosses, when it runs, the protocol every foreign process speaks, and the SDK it's written with. JS and TS come first; the protocol is language-neutral, so other runtimes can follow with their own SDKs.
